# Bride kit — the POLYGON half of the bride, authored in WAM.
#
# WHY TWO LANGUAGES: goblin-kit.wam's header, and the owner's rule
# (2026-09-08): flesh is SDF, armour and accessories are MESH. Plate wants
# edges smooth-min cannot keep; her flesh wants exactly the roundness it gives.
#
# WHAT SHE WEARS (spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-bride-sword-enemy-design.md):
#   * PLATE (dull steel, `plate` = breakable armour, webgpu/kit-damage.ts):
#     vambraces on both forearms, couters cupping the backs of both elbows,
#     fingered gauntlets on both hands, and ONE pauldron, on the RIGHT (sword)
#     shoulder. The left shoulder and both upper arms stay bare.
#   * BOOT: cream suede thigh-highs.
#   * CHAIN: a chain girdle over the skirt's waist, a choker and a long
#     necklace that falls onto the top of the bodice slot.
#   * IRON: three crosses: two hanging off the girdle, one off the necklace,
#     dangling over the laced rib window.
#
# HOOK 4, THE FUSED GAUNTLETS (bride.blob's header). The plate is built
# AROUND raw-red flesh the .blob already grows, and must never cover it:
#   * the ELBOW CREASE (upperarm at=1.00, +z): the couter cups only the BACK
#     of the elbow and the vambrace starts 4-5 cm below the joint, so the
#     front of the elbow is an open, red seam between two plates;
#   * UNDER THE PAULDRON (upperarm.r at=0.24-0.30): the pauldron's skirt ends
#     at y ~1.37, above the two swellings, and is open underneath (no cap) —
#     the red flesh bulges out from under the rim;
#   * THE SWORD-HAND CUFF (forearm.r at=0.97, hand.r's tendril): the right
#     vambrace stops short of the wrist and the right gauntlet is a back-of-
#     hand plate whose fingers sink into the flesh, so the red wrist ring
#     and the tendril that grows on past the fist (toward the sword grip,
#     Task 5) both show.
#
# THE SKELETON BELOW MIRRORS characters/bride.blob AND MUST TRACK IT.
# bride-kit.test.ts checks every bone head to 10 mm. The two conversions
# from goblin-kit.wam's header, neither optional:
#   * UNITS. WAM lengths are fractions of `height`; .blob's are metres. The
#     bride's height is 1.85 (bride.blob's `height`), so every number here —
#     bones, rings, offsets, attach sizes — is the metre value / 1.85. (The
#     compiled glTF is in metres again: WAM multiplies back by `height`.)
#   * PITCH SIGN ON `down` BONES. Up bones share pitch verbatim; every down
#     bone NEGATES it. tilt needs no flip.
#
# THE UNEVEN FOREARM. bride.blob gives the sword forearm its own length
# (`forearm len=0.26 lenR=0.30`); a WAM mirror block always gives .l and .r
# one length (wam/skeleton.py solve()). So forearm.l / forearm.r are written
# OUT of the mirror, as explicit sided bones parented to the mirrored
# upperarm.l / upperarm.r (WAM resolves `parent=upperarm.r` literally; checked
# with a ten-line test .wam first). Being outside the mirror, the .r bone
# is not reflected for us: its tilt is written NEGATIVE by hand (tilt splays
# a down bone toward +x, and the right arm splays toward -x). The hands then
# go back in a second mirror block, whose `parent=forearm` resolves to the
# suffixed forearm.l / forearm.r.
#
# FLESH THIS WRAPS, marched off bride.blob with sdBody bisects PER LIMB-
# ISOLATED CLUSTER (the soldier's method; arms after the 2026-09-24 splay),
# as the RADIUS from the bone axis, in METRES:
#   forearm (both; t is the fraction of each side's own length)
#     t0.10 0.032  t0.20 0.029  t0.40 0.027  t0.60 0.0255  t0.80 0.0235
#     t0.90 0.023 (L) / 0.025 (R)  t1.00 0.026 (L) / 0.036 (R: the red cuff)
#   hand.l  t0.20 w0.040 d0.052  t0.45 w0.036 d0.055  t0.70 w0.026 d0.040,
#           flesh ends at ~t0.8 (y 0.80)
#   hand.r  t0.00 w0.072 d0.073  t0.45 w0.059 d0.068  t1.00 0.045, the
#           tendril on to t1.6 (0.034)
#   elbow   w0.074 d0.083 (the crease bulge is +0.047 in front)
#   deltoid upperarm t0.10 0.044, t0.30 0.036 (the .r bulges reach 0.05)
#   thigh   t0.58 0.052  t0.70 0.050  t0.90 0.043  knee 0.041
#   shin    t0.10 0.033  t0.20 w0.082 d0.089 (calf, -z 0.050)  t0.30 w0.078
#           d0.084  t0.40 0.037  t0.50 0.031  t0.60 0.026  t0.80 0.023
#           t1.00 0.022
#   foot    flesh x 0.054..0.116, y 0.012..~0.05, z -0.030..0.136 (ankle
#           at x 0.085, y 0.071)
#   girdle  skirt dome at y 1.070: half-width 0.175, half-depth 0.164
#   neck    t0.30 w0.081 d0.085; the shoulder yoke tops out at y 1.466
#   chest   front surface z at x=0: y1.44 0.049, 1.41 0.072, 1.38 0.105,
#           1.35 0.111 (the bodice top / bust)
#
# RING MARGINS. `style chunky` lofts are 8-sided and a facet midpoint sits
# at cos(22.5) = 92.4% of the nominal radius, so every plate ring is
# (flesh / 0.924) + ~6 mm. The boots are 12-sided (cos 15 = 96.6%) — suede,
# not plate — at ~+7 mm.
#
# SKIRT CLEARANCE. The vambraces hang beside the ruffle skirt's widest tier.
# With the Task 1 arm hang (upperarm tilt 11, forearm 6) the forearm FLESH
# already ran 5-14 mm into the skirt at y 0.94-1.04 (probed at the forearm's
# own z), so any plate there punched straight through it. bride.blob's arms
# now splay to tilt 14 / 12: flesh-to-skirt clearance is >= 13 mm at rest,
# and the vambrace's ~6 mm margin leaves the plate clear of the cloth.
#
# BUILD:  scripts/build-wam-kit.sh bride
#   -> public/assets/lab/bride-kit.gltf (committed; WAM lives outside the repo).
#
# EXPECTED LINTS, correct to ignore: bones with no geometry near them (the
# flesh lives in the .blob — pelvis, spine1, chest, skull, upperarm.l,
# clavicle, ...).
model bride-kit
  height 1.85
  style chunky

palette
  # DULL STEEL. A neutral grey (no hue to go blue under the env sheen; the
  # soldier kit's note). kit-overlay.ts gives BREAKABLE plate its own duller
  # look (metalness 0.70, roughness 0.24), which is the brief: worn, not
  # mirror-bright — the shine in her read belongs to the wet red seams.
  plate #6c7075
  # CREAM SUEDE. A warm cream, a step darker than the ivory stockings
  # (e8e0d0) and skirt (f4f1ea), so the boot top reads as a separate layer
  # against the stocking band rather than as more stocking.
  boot  #c9b48e
  # Chains: darkened steel, a step below the plate so the fine links read
  # against it. kit-overlay.ts LOOK gives `chain` the iron sheen.
  chain #4c4f54
  # Blackened iron crosses.
  iron  #34363a

skeleton
  # .blob `root pelvis at 0.96 len=0.08` -> a WAM root POINT + `hips`.
  # 0.96/1.85, 0.08/1.85. Every .blob `parent=pelvis` becomes `parent=hips`.
  root pelvis at 0.51892
  bone hips   parent=pelvis dir=up len=0.04324
  # up-bone pitches verbatim.
  bone spine1 parent=hips   dir=up pitch=-2 len=0.08108
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=-3 len=0.09189
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=0  len=0.03784
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=8  len=0.07568
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=-4 len=0.12973
  # THE HEM PENDULUM (bride.blob, Task 3): a down bone from the hip joint
  # whose tail is a loose Verlet point; the rigid ruffle skirt rides it. It
  # is transcribed because the girdle and its crosses ride it TOO — a chain
  # on the hips would be crossed by the swinging skirt every stride.
  bone hem    parent=hips   dir=down len=0.21622
  mirror
    # clavicle dir=side: tilt verbatim (toward +y on both languages).
    bone clavicle parent=spine2   side=0.01081 dir=side tilt=-8 len=0.07027
    # down: .blob upperarm tilt 14 pitch 2 -> pitch -2.
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=14 pitch=-2 len=0.16216
    # down: .blob thigh pitch 2 -> -2, shin -1 -> 1.
    bone thigh    parent=hips     dir=down tilt=-1.5 pitch=-2 side=0.04595 len=0.26486
    bone shin     parent=thigh    dir=down tilt=1.5  pitch=1  len=0.25946
    bone foot     parent=shin     dir=fwd                     len=0.07027
  end
  # THE UNEVEN FOREARM (see the header): .blob `forearm tilt=12 pitch=10
  # len=0.26 lenR=0.30`. pitch negated (down bone); .r's tilt negated by
  # hand because nothing mirrors it.
  bone forearm.l parent=upperarm.l dir=down tilt=12  pitch=-10 len=0.14054
  bone forearm.r parent=upperarm.r dir=down tilt=-12 pitch=-10 len=0.16216
  mirror
    # .blob hand pitch 8 -> -8. `parent=forearm` resolves forearm.l / .r.
    bone hand parent=forearm dir=down pitch=-8 len=0.04324
  end
  # KIT-ONLY BONES: the long necklace's path, which no blob bone follows.
  # A chain of short bones hung off spine2's tail, running from behind the
  # left side of the neck, over the collarbone, down to the top of the bodice
  # slot (x 0, y 1.362, z 0.118) and back up the right side. Each point sits
  # ~6-8 mm off the probed chest surface. The rig has no frames for these
  # names, so kit-overlay.ts poses them from their parent (spine2) — they
  # ride the upper chest rigidly, which is what a necklace lying on it does.
  #   P0 ( 0.050, 1.472, -0.020)  P1 ( 0.062, 1.452, 0.040)
  #   P2 ( 0.048, 1.412,  0.074)  P3 ( 0.024, 1.378, 0.108)
  #   P4 ( 0.000, 1.362,  0.118)  ... and back, x mirrored.
  bone nk0 parent=spine2 at=1.0 offset=(0.02703,0.02286,-0.00319) dir=(0.1864,-0.3107,0.9321) len=0.0348
  bone nk1 parent=nk0 dir=(-0.2577,-0.7362,0.6258) len=0.02937
  bone nk2 parent=nk1 dir=(-0.4466,-0.6327,0.6327) len=0.02905
  bone nk3 parent=nk2 dir=(-0.7861,-0.5241,0.3276) len=0.0165
  bone nk4 parent=nk3 dir=(-0.7861,0.5241,-0.3276) len=0.0165
  bone nk5 parent=nk4 dir=(-0.4466,0.6327,-0.6327) len=0.02905
  bone nk6 parent=nk5 dir=(-0.2577,0.7362,-0.6258) len=0.02937
  bone nk7 parent=nk6 dir=(0.1864,0.3107,-0.9321) len=0.0348

parts
  # ==========================================================================
  # VAMBRACES — plate tubes on both forearms, from 4-5 cm below the elbow
  # (the crease stays OPEN) to the wrist. (flesh / 0.924) + 6 mm per ring.
  # Written per side, not mirrored: the rings are the same fractions, but the
  # sword side stops SHORT of the wrist so the red cuff (forearm.r at=0.97)
  # shows between it and the gauntlet, while the off side runs on under the
  # gauntlet's flared cuff.
  # The rings beside the skirt are 2 mm narrower and sit 3 mm OUTWARD
  # (side=, which is world +x on a down bone, so negative on the right arm):
  # the plate stays full on the outside and hugs the flesh (~4 mm) on the
  # inside, where the ruffle skirt's warp came within 1-2 mm of it at rest.
  # ==========================================================================
  loft vambrace.l bones=forearm.l..forearm.l material=plate
    ring 0.17 w=0.04324 d=0.04324
    ring 0.22 w=0.04054 d=0.04162 side=0.00162
    ring 0.45 w=0.0373 d=0.03838 side=0.00162
    ring 0.70 w=0.03459 d=0.03568 side=0.00162
    ring 0.90 w=0.03351 d=0.03405 side=0.00108
    ring 0.98 w=0.03676 d=0.03784
    cap start=none end=none
  loft vambrace.r bones=forearm.r..forearm.r material=plate
    ring 0.15 w=0.04324 d=0.04324
    ring 0.20 w=0.04054 d=0.04162 side=-0.00162
    ring 0.43 w=0.0373 d=0.03838 side=-0.00162
    ring 0.68 w=0.03459 d=0.03568 side=-0.00162
    ring 0.84 w=0.03459 d=0.03514 side=-0.00108
    ring 0.88 w=0.03784 d=0.03892
    cap start=none end=none

  mirror
    # ========================================================================
    # COUTERS — a cup over the BACK of each elbow, never the front: a free ray
    # from the elbow joint aimed back (-z) and a little outward, starting
    # 10 mm behind the joint so the rim rides the sides of the joint and the
    # crease in front stays bare. The rim ring is buried in the arm above and
    # below the joint (that is where a couter's lames tuck), the apex stands
    # ~15 mm off the point of the elbow. yaw=-25 turns a back-pointing ray
    # toward +x (outward on .l; mirrored for .r).
    # ========================================================================
    loft couter bone=upperarm at=1.0 offset=(0,0,-0.00541) dir=back yaw=-25 len=0.02432 material=plate
      ring 0.00 w=0.05297 d=0.06054
      ring 0.45 w=0.04757 d=0.05297
      ring 0.80 w=0.03459 d=0.03892
      ring 1.00 w=0.02162 d=0.02486
      cap start=none end=dome

    # ========================================================================
    # THIGH-HIGH BOOTS — cream suede from y ~0.756 (thigh t0.58) down to the
    # ankle, 12-sided (suede, not plate). The top sits 2-3 cm UNDER the
    # stocking's lace band (y 0.77-0.79), so a strip of ivory stocking and the
    # band show between boot and skirt hem (0.855). A folded cuff at the top.
    # Chain t = thigh 0.49 + shin 0.48; the knee is at chain t 0.505. The calf
    # rings carry the flesh's backward swell (fwd<0).
    # ========================================================================
    loft bootshaft bones=thigh..shin material=boot sides=12
      ring 0.293 w=0.07135 d=0.07405
      ring 0.306 w=0.07027 d=0.07297
      ring 0.318 w=0.06595 d=0.06919
      ring 0.354 w=0.06378 d=0.06703
      ring 0.455 w=0.05568 d=0.05838
      ring 0.505 w=0.05405 d=0.05622
      ring 0.555 w=0.04649 d=0.04757
      ring 0.604 w=0.05405 d=0.06162 fwd=-0.00324
      ring 0.653 w=0.05189 d=0.05838 fwd=-0.0027
      ring 0.703 w=0.04865 d=0.05189 fwd=-0.00162
      ring 0.752 w=0.04324 d=0.04432
      ring 0.802 w=0.03784 d=0.03784
      ring 0.901 w=0.03459 d=0.03459
      ring 1.000 w=0.03351 d=0.03459
      cap start=none end=none

    # BOOT FOOT — a free ray along +z from behind the heel to past the toe,
    # frame=up so d is HEIGHT. Centre y 0.040 (offset -0.031 from the 0.0707
    # ankle), so the tallest ring (0.080) puts the sole on y 0.000. Starts
    # 45 mm behind the ankle, runs 200 mm to a pointed toe 10 mm past the
    # flesh. The ankle rings swallow the shaft's bottom ring.
    loft bootfoot bone=foot at=0.0 offset=(0,-0.01676,-0.02919) dir=fwd len=0.10811 frame=up material=boot sides=12
      ring 0.00 w=0.02703 d=0.03243
      ring 0.10 w=0.03892 d=0.04324
      ring 0.30 w=0.04216 d=0.04324
      ring 0.55 w=0.04216 d=0.03459
      ring 0.78 w=0.03784 d=0.02703
      ring 0.93 w=0.02703 d=0.02162
      ring 1.00 w=0.01405 d=0.01622
      cap start=flat end=flat
  end

  # ==========================================================================
  # GAUNTLETS. The off hand: a full fingered gauntlet — a flared cuff over
  # the vambrace's end, a plated back of hand, and four articulated claws
  # (plus a thumb) that run on 3-4 cm past the flesh fingers: plate hands
  # that end in points. The hand hangs palm-in, so the fingers stand in a
  # row along z (index in front).
  # ==========================================================================
  loft gauntlet.l bones=hand.l..hand.l material=plate
    ring 0.00 w=0.03459 d=0.04
    ring 0.12 w=0.03027 d=0.03784
    ring 0.40 w=0.02703 d=0.03676
    ring 0.62 w=0.02378 d=0.03351
    cap start=none end=none
  loft finger1.l bone=hand.l at=0.55 offset=(-0.00108,0,0.00973) dir=down tilt=-6 pitch=6 len=0.03135 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00757 d=0.00703
    ring 0.50 w=0.00649 d=0.00649
    ring 1.00 w=0.00108 d=0.00108 tip
    cap start=none end=none
  loft finger2.l bone=hand.l at=0.55 offset=(-0.00108,0,0.00324) dir=down tilt=-6 pitch=2 len=0.03459 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00757 d=0.00703
    ring 0.50 w=0.00649 d=0.00649
    ring 1.00 w=0.00108 d=0.00108 tip
    cap start=none end=none
  loft finger3.l bone=hand.l at=0.55 offset=(-0.00108,0,-0.00324) dir=down tilt=-6 pitch=-2 len=0.03243 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00757 d=0.00703
    ring 0.50 w=0.00649 d=0.00649
    ring 1.00 w=0.00108 d=0.00108 tip
    cap start=none end=none
  loft finger4.l bone=hand.l at=0.55 offset=(-0.00108,0,-0.00973) dir=down tilt=-6 pitch=-6 len=0.02703 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00703 d=0.00649
    ring 0.50 w=0.00595 d=0.00595
    ring 1.00 w=0.00108 d=0.00108 tip
    cap start=none end=none
  loft thumb.l bone=hand.l at=0.25 offset=(-0.00216,0,0.01405) dir=down tilt=-12 pitch=-30 len=0.02432 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00865 d=0.00811
    ring 0.50 w=0.00703 d=0.00703
    ring 1.00 w=0.00108 d=0.00108 tip
    cap start=none end=none

  # The SWORD hand: a plated back of hand only, starting past the red wrist
  # cuff, open at the end, with the flesh tendril (hand.r at=0.10 -> 12.5 cm
  # on, toward the grip) growing out of it. Four short plated fingers curl
  # into that flesh and sink there: the hand cannot let go.
  loft gauntlet.r bones=hand.r..hand.r material=plate
    ring 0.10 w=0.04216 d=0.04432
    ring 0.35 w=0.03892 d=0.04324
    ring 0.62 w=0.03568 d=0.04
    cap start=none end=none
  loft finger1.r bone=hand.r at=0.55 offset=(0,0,0.01081) dir=down tilt=14 pitch=4 len=0.01946 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00865 d=0.00811
    ring 1.00 w=0.00649 d=0.00649
    cap start=none end=flat
  loft finger2.r bone=hand.r at=0.55 offset=(0,0,0.00378) dir=down tilt=14 len=0.02162 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00865 d=0.00811
    ring 1.00 w=0.00649 d=0.00649
    cap start=none end=flat
  loft finger3.r bone=hand.r at=0.55 offset=(0,0,-0.00378) dir=down tilt=14 len=0.02054 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00865 d=0.00811
    ring 1.00 w=0.00649 d=0.00649
    cap start=none end=flat
  loft finger4.r bone=hand.r at=0.55 offset=(0,0,-0.01081) dir=down tilt=14 pitch=-4 len=0.0173 material=plate shape=squarish
    ring 0.00 w=0.00811 d=0.00757
    ring 1.00 w=0.00595 d=0.00595
    cap start=none end=flat

  # ==========================================================================
  # PAULDRON — the RIGHT (sword) shoulder only. A domed shell over the
  # deltoid, on a free ray down the upper arm starting 55 mm above the
  # shoulder socket, its skirt flaring to a lip that ends at y ~1.37, ABOVE
  # the two raw-red swellings (upperarm.r at=0.24-0.30, y 1.32-1.34, reaching
  # 0.05 off the arm axis). No bottom cap: the underside is open and the red
  # flesh bulges out from under the lip. tilt=-6 is the right side's
  # outward lean, written by hand (nothing mirrors it); pitch -2 is the
  # upper arm's (negated). A tall flange (haute-piece) stands on its inner
  # edge beside the neck: the death-knight silhouette.
  # ==========================================================================
  loft pauldron bone=upperarm.r at=0.0 offset=(-0.00649,0.02811,0) dir=down tilt=-6 pitch=-2 len=0.05405 material=plate
    ring 0.00 w=0.03351 d=0.03243
    ring 0.22 w=0.0627 d=0.05838
    ring 0.50 w=0.07351 d=0.06703
    ring 0.80 w=0.07784 d=0.07027
    ring 1.00 w=0.08432 d=0.07568
    cap start=dome end=none
  attach hautepiece bone=upperarm.r kind=box at=0.0 offset=(0.01514,0.04432,0) w=0.00378 h=0.02162 d=0.04973 taper=1.15 material=plate

  # ==========================================================================
  # CHAINS
  # ==========================================================================
  # GIRDLE — a chain band over the skirt's waist (the dome top, y ~1.070),
  # riding the HEM pendulum with the skirt so the two never cross. 16-sided
  # for a round band; a 10 mm band with a rolled edge (the mid ring proud).
  # Sized to the probed skirt: half-width 0.175, half-depth 0.164 at 1.070.
  loft girdle bone=hem at=0.0 offset=(0,0.01892,0) dir=down len=0.00541 frame=fwd material=chain sides=16
    ring 0.00 w=0.19676 d=0.18595
    ring 0.50 w=0.20432 d=0.19351
    ring 1.00 w=0.20541 d=0.19459
    cap start=none end=none

  # CHOKER — a thin chain round the neck at neck t0.63 (y ~1.517), just ABOVE
  # the painted throat cross (y 1.47-1.506), which bleeds out from under it.
  # Lower was tried first: at t0.30 the whole ring sat 12 mm inside the
  # shoulder yoke, which rises to y 1.466 either side of the neck. Neck flesh
  # w 0.075 d 0.079 here.
  loft choker bones=neck..neck material=chain sides=12
    ring 0.60 w=0.04649 d=0.04865
    ring 0.63 w=0.04919 d=0.05135
    ring 0.66 w=0.04595 d=0.04811
    cap start=none end=none

  # LONG NECKLACE — a 9 mm chain along the nk0..nk7 path (skeleton above).
  loft necklace bones=nk0..nk7 material=chain sides=6
    ring 0.00 w=0.00486 d=0.00486
    ring 1.00 w=0.00486 d=0.00486
    cap start=flat end=flat

  # ==========================================================================
  # IRON CROSSES. Each is two boxes in a group's own frame (the upright hangs
  # DOWN from the origin — a box's top face sits at its origin), mounted by
  # aiming the group's +Y.
  # ==========================================================================
  # The necklace cross: hangs from the necklace's lowest point (P4, the top
  # of the bodice slot), in the gap between the bust, over the laces.
  group ncross bone=nk3 at=1.0 offset=(0,-0.00216,0.00162) dir=up pitch=-8
    attach nbail kind=box offset=(0,0.00216,0) w=0.00216 h=0.00432 d=0.00216 material=iron
    attach nup kind=box offset=(0,-0.00216,0) w=0.00541 h=0.03027 d=0.00324 material=iron
    attach nbar kind=box offset=(0,-0.00919,0) w=0.01946 h=0.00541 d=0.00324 material=iron
  end
  # The girdle crosses: two hanging from its front, left and right of centre,
  # each turned to the skirt's surface normal there (spin) and leaned back
  # with the bell (pitch). A short link ties each to the band.
  group gcross.l bone=hem at=0.0 offset=(0.03892,0.01243,0.09946) dir=up pitch=-14 spin=-21
    attach glink.l kind=box offset=(0,0.00649,0) w=0.00216 h=0.00757 d=0.00216 material=chain
